---
const vanillaPseudo = [
  "for k = 1, 2, …, K:",
  "    g_k, h_k = ∇L(F_k),  H(F_k)",
  "    f_k = NewtonTree(g_k, h_k, λ_base)",
  "    F_{k+1} = F_k + η · f_k",
];

const grnPseudo = [
  "for k = 1, 2, …, K:",
  "    g_k, h_k = ∇L(F_k),  H(F_k)",
  "    λ_k = λ_base + √(M·||g_k||_H)",
  "    f_k = NewtonTree(g_k, h_k, λ_k)",
  "    F_{k+1} = F_k + η · f_k",
];
---

<section id="algorithms" class="section relative">
  <div aria-hidden="true" class="absolute inset-0 -z-10 bg-bg-deep/60"></div>
  <div class="container-page">
    <div class="reveal max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Algorithms</p>
      <h2 class="mt-4 font-display text-display-lg text-balance text-ink">
        Two engines. One elegant difference.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
        Vanilla Newton boosting (Algorithm 1) and Gradient Regularized Newton
        boosting (Algorithm 2) share everything &mdash; loss, tree builder,
        diagnostics &mdash; except a single line that changes the entire
        convergence behaviour.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-14 grid grid-cols-1 gap-5 lg:grid-cols-2">
      <!-- Vanilla -->
      <article class="reveal card flex flex-col overflow-hidden">
        <header class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-7 pt-7">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
            <span
              class="grid h-7 w-7 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-signal-red/10 text-signal-red"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M12 9v4M12 17h.01" />
                <path d="M10.29 3.86 1.82 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.71 3h16.94a2 2 0 0 0 1.71-3L13.71 3.86a2 2 0 0 0-3.42 0Z" />
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[1.0625rem] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
              Vanilla Newton Boosting
            </h3>
          </div>
          <span class="chip">
            <span class="inline-block h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-signal-red"></span>
            Static λ
          </span>
        </header>

        <div class="px-7 pt-4">
          <p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Algorithm 1. Uses a fixed λ<sub>base</sub> at every iteration. On
            losses with non-constant Hessians &mdash; e.g. Charbonnier or
            cross-entropy &mdash; the iteration can <strong>diverge</strong>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <pre class="mx-7 mt-5 mb-7 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-bg-deep/70 p-5 font-mono text-[12.5px] leading-[1.7] text-ink-muted">
{vanillaPseudo.join("\n")}</pre>

        <footer class="mt-auto flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-t border-line bg-bg-deep/40 px-7 py-4 text-[12.5px] text-ink-soft">
          <span>Paper §3 · Algorithm 1</span>
          <code class="font-mono text-ink-muted">λ_base</code>
        </footer>
      </article>

      <!-- GRN -->
      <article
        class="reveal card relative flex flex-col overflow-hidden"
        style="animation-delay: 120ms;"
      >
        <span
          class="absolute right-5 top-5 inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-full bg-gradient-brand px-2.5 py-1 text-[10.5px] font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-white"
        >
          <svg class="h-3 w-3" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7" />
          </svg>
          Recommended
        </span>
        <header class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 px-7 pt-7">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5">
            <span
              class="grid h-7 w-7 place-items-center rounded-lg bg-signal-green/10 text-signal-green"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5" />
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[1.0625rem] font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">
              Gradient Regularized Newton
            </h3>
          </div>
          <span class="chip">
            <span class="inline-block h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-signal-green"></span>
            Adaptive λ<sub>k</sub>
          </span>
        </header>

        <div class="px-7 pt-4">
          <p class="text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-ink-muted">
            Algorithm 2. λ<sub>k</sub> scales with the gradient norm
            (Proposition 5.1). The iteration <strong>converges</strong> &mdash;
            steadily and provably.
          </p>
        </div>

        <pre class="mx-7 mt-5 mb-7 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-line bg-bg-deep/70 p-5 font-mono text-[12.5px] leading-[1.7] text-ink">
{grnPseudo.join("\n")}
        </pre>

        <footer
          class="mt-auto flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-t border-line bg-bg-deep/40 px-7 py-4 text-[12.5px] text-ink-soft"
        >
          <span>Paper §5 · Algorithm 2</span>
          <code class="font-mono text-ink-muted">λ<sub>k</sub> = λ<sub>base</sub> + √(M · ||g<sub>k</sub>||<sub>H</sub>)</code>
        </footer>
      </article>
    </div>

    <!-- The key insight strip -->
    <div class="reveal mt-10 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="card p-6">
        <div class="eyebrow">Closed-form leaf</div>
        <p class="mt-3 font-display text-display-sm text-ink">
          <code class="font-mono text-[1.05rem] text-accent-500">w = -Σg / (Σh + λ)</code>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Algorithm 1, line 4 &mdash; exact, no gradient descent on leaves.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card p-6">
        <div class="eyebrow">Exact Newton gain</div>
        <p class="mt-3 font-display text-display-sm text-ink">
          <code class="font-mono text-[1rem] text-accent-500">½[ G²_L/(H_L+λ) + … − G²/(H+λ) ]</code>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Used for greedy split selection; closed form, no approximations.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="card p-6">
        <div class="eyebrow">Lipschitz M<sub>0</sub></div>
        <p class="mt-3 font-display text-display-sm text-ink">
          <code class="font-mono text-[1.05rem] text-accent-500">M<sub>0</sub> &isin; &#123;0, &frac14;, 1&#125;</code>
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Analytic Hessian-Lipschitz constants for MSE, BCE/CCE and Charbonnier.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
